  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nGiven:\n\n(5, 9, 52)\n\n__**(9 × 5)**__ + 5 + 2 = 52\n\n__**45 + 5 + 2**__ = 52 \n\n52 = 52 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n(11, 7, 90)\n\n__(11 × 7)__ + 11 + 2 = 90\n\n__77 + 11 + 2__ = 90\n\n90 = 90 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo, checking each option one by one:\n\nOption 1) (7, 13, 98)\n\n__(7 × 13)__ + 7 + 2 = 98\n\n__91 + 7 + 2__ = 98\n\n100 ≠ 98 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 2) (14, 4, 63)\n\n__(14 × 4)__ + 14 + 2 = 63\n\n__56 + 14 + 2__ = 63\n\n72 ≠ 63 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 3) (8, 11, 95)\n\n__(8 × 11)__ + 8 + 2 = 95\n\n__88 + 8 + 2__ = 95\n\n98 ≠ 95 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 4) (9, 6, 65) \n\n__(9 × 6)__ + 9 + 2 = 65\n\n__54 + 9 + 2__ = 65\n\n**65 = 65 (LHS = RHS)**\n\nThus, out of all the options, '(9, 6, 65) ' follows the same logic as given.\n\nHence, \"Option 4\" is the correct answer.",
